From df0b7b0b420c0f15ccb0a1e870cce23b26cc7ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:45:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report SAP asset progress honestly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A real diagnostic report came back reading stage: assets, percent: 100 with no
error, which looks like a stall at 100% and is not one. The four binaries
download in parallel and differ in size by two orders of magnitude, and each
reported its own loaded/total, so the screen said 100% the moment the 207 KB
one landed — with the 29 MB one barely started and most of the wait still ahead.

Progress is now one number: bytes in hand over bytes expected, sized up front
with a HEAD per file. When the total cannot be known it falls back to per-file
numbers rather than computing a percentage against a wrong denominator.

The server's own fetch from Apple was also being pushed through that channel as
loaded=found/total=4, where it read as a byte percentage — so it showed 100%
before a single byte had been downloaded. It gets its own installing stage with
no percentage, since there is no honest one to give.

Verified by reverting the accumulation and watching the new tests fail with
'expected 100 to be less than 50'.

Also documents that DATA_DIR must not live under /tmp — a deployment that does
loses the 38 MB on every restart and re-downloads it, which on a slow uplink
looks exactly like a hang at sign-in — and that BUILD_COMMIT needs passing at
build time, without which every deployment reports 'unknown'.
